{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "macros.html.j2" as m %}
{% block content %}
{% set latest = years[-1] %}
{% set p = pooled or latest %}
<h1>{{ page.title }}</h1>
<p class="lede">Every year the American Society of Human Genetics picks a few hundred of its several thousand accepted
abstracts for a talk; the rest become posters. This site parses the published abstract booklets
({{ years[0].year }}–{{ latest.year }}) and asks which phrases, institutions and places show up more often among talks.</p>
<p class="caveat"><strong>Read this first.</strong> The booklets list only <em>accepted</em> abstracts, and authors
can ask for a poster. "Talk rate" is the fraction of accepted abstracts presented as a talk, not an acceptance
rate or a quality score. Every number here is an association.</p>

{{ m.figure("img/%s_headline.png" % ("all" if pooled else latest.year), "Dot plot of the phrases most over-represented in ASHG %s talks versus posters, with odds ratios and 95%% confidence intervals." % p.label) }}
<p>{% if pooled %}Over all {{ years | length }} meetings ({{ "{:,}".format(p.summary.abstracts) }} abstracts,
{{ "{:,}".format(p.summary.talks) }} talks), {% endif %}talks over-index on
“{{ p.top_phrases.talk | join("”, “") }}”; posters on “{{ p.top_phrases.poster | join("”, “") }}”.
<a href="phrases.html">Each year, phrase trends and a phrase lookup →</a></p>

{% if "trends_talk_rate" in trends %}
<h2 id="talk-rate">Talk rate by year</h2>
<p>The share of accepted abstracts presented as a talk ranges from
{{ "%.1f"|format(100 * (years | map(attribute="summary.talk_rate") | min)) }}% to
{{ "%.1f"|format(100 * (years | map(attribute="summary.talk_rate") | max)) }}% by year. Every talk rate on this site is
compared with its own year's rate, or with the pooled rate for all years.</p>
{{ m.figure("img/trends_talk_rate.png", "Talk rate per year: the share of accepted abstracts presented as a talk, with each year's talk and abstract counts and host city.") }}
{% endif %}

<h2 id="explore">Explore</h2>
<p>Each page has a year toggle: all years pooled, or one meeting at a time.</p>
<div class="cards">
  <a class="card" href="phrases.html">
    <img src="img/trends_phrases.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Phrases</h3>
    <p>Phrases that predict a talk, how they trend year to year, a lookup for any phrase, and sample sizes in talks
    versus posters.</p><span class="more">Phrases →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="institutions.html">
    <img src="img/{{ 'all' if pooled else latest.year }}_institutions.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Institutions</h3>
    <p>Which of the largest institutions have the highest talk rate, crediting the first author.</p>
    <span class="more">Institutions →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="geography.html">
    <img src="img/{{ 'all' if pooled else latest.year }}_regions.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Geography</h3>
    <p>Talk rate by world region, country and metro area, including the host-city effect.</p>
    <span class="more">Regions, countries and metros →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card" href="authors.html">
    <img src="img/{{ 'all' if pooled else latest.year }}_senior_authors.png" alt="" loading="lazy">
    <div class="body"><h3>Senior authors</h3>
    <p>Senior authors with the most consistent record of talks, ranked by the lower end of a 95% interval.</p>
    <span class="more">Senior authors →</span></div>
  </a>
  <a class="card text-only" href="methods.html">
    <div class="body"><h3>Methods and caveats</h3>
    <p>How the booklets are parsed, how institutions and places are resolved, how phrases are scored, and what
    the numbers can't tell you.</p><span class="more">Methods →</span></div>
  </a>
</div>
{% endblock %}
